1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:11,350
March 1989. Mark Kilroy, a twenty-one-year-old pre-med student from the University of Texas, crossed into Matamoros for spring break with his friends.

2
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:18,760
Fifteen thousand spring breakers crowded the streets that night. Around two in the morning, outside a bar, Mark vanished.

3
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:30,400
His friends searched until dawn. His parents printed twenty thousand flyers, offered a fifteen-thousand-dollar reward, and took the case to national television. For weeks, nothing.

4
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:42,120
Then, on April 1st, a drug trafficker named Serafín Hernández drove straight through a police checkpoint. According to later accounts, he believed rituals had made him invisible.

5
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:51,590
Federal police followed him to a ranch outside the city: Rancho Santa Elena. Inside, they found ritual objects and traces of drugs.

6
00:00:51,610 --> 00:01:02,610
Days later, they arrested Serafín, his uncle Elio, and three others. Serafín confessed: people had been killed at the ranch, on the orders of a man they called El Padrino.

7
00:01:02,630 --> 00:01:10,310
Police dug up a ritual cauldron… and fifteen bodies, most of them rival traffickers. One of them was Mark Kilroy.

8
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:21,240
El Padrino was Adolfo de Jesús Constanzo, born in Miami in 1962. His mother practiced Palo Mayombe, and he grew up steeped in ritual.

9
00:01:21,260 --> 00:01:29,070
In Mexico City, he read tarot cards for wealthy clients, among them drug dealers and, reportedly, corrupt police.

10
00:01:29,090 --> 00:01:41,460
Then he made a deal with a trafficking family: a share of their profits, in exchange for his protection. He promised his followers that human sacrifice would protect them from bullets and from the police.

11
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:49,650
His second-in-command was Sara Aldrete, a top student from just across the border. Followers called her La Madrina.

12
00:01:49,670 --> 00:01:59,170
Weeks later, police cornered Constanzo in Mexico City. On May 6th, 1989, he ordered one of his own followers to shoot him.

13
00:01:59,190 --> 00:02:08,420
Aldrete was arrested at the scene. In 1994, she was sentenced to more than sixty years in prison. She still insists she is innocent.

14
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:14,630
Mark's parents started a foundation in his name, teaching young people about the dangers of drugs.

15
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:25,632
No trial for El Padrino. No answers. The cult that thought it was invisible was exposed by the one family that wouldn't stop looking. This is Plot Twist with A&R.

